screen.LEISTUNG.comment = Everything that costs frame rate, sorted by measured impact - try the top entries first. The largest items are the cloud march steps and the shadow sampling.
screen.BILD.comment = Bloom, anti-aliasing and ambient occlusion. The colouring of twilight is now under Sky & clouds.
screen.HIMMEL.comment = The two most important sliders at the top, everything else by topic below: cloud shape, cloud light, weather, cloud shadows, twilight, sun and moon, aurora and light shafts.
screen.MOND.comment = Size, brightness and surface of the procedural moon, plus the switch back to the vanilla textures.
screen.LICHT.comment = Shadow colour and softness, cave lighting, gloss and reflections on blocks. Shadow map fine-tuning lives under Expert.
screen.WASSER.comment = Clarity, waves, wind, sun glitter and caustics. Shore foam lives under Experimental.
screen.WELT.comment = Cold fog, precipitation and puddles, thunderstorms, brightness in the Nether and the End.
screen.EXPERIMENTELL.comment = Fully built and tuned, but deliberately NOT on by default - either because it is a matter of taste or because it costs performance. Switching it on gives you the tuned values.
screen.EXPERTE.comment = Internals of the calculation. Not normally needed; the values are tuned against each other and changing one alone can make the image worse.
screen.XWOLKEN.comment = Shape, swirl, scattering and cirrus in detail, plus the A/B switches of the cloud calculation.
screen.XSCHATTEN.comment = Distortion, bias and edge handling of the shadow map. These values have several rounds of tuning behind them.
screen.XWASSER.comment = Noise construction of the waves and fine-tuning of block reflections.
screen.XBILD.comment = Fine-tuning of anti-aliasing and ambient occlusion.
screen.DIAGNOSE.comment = Diagnostic views for troubleshooting. They show individual quantities raw on screen - all off during normal play.

option.CLOUD_OFF_DEBUG = Disable cloud pass
option.CLOUD_OFF_DEBUG.comment = Removes the clouds from the image entirely while leaving everything else untouched - unlike the other diagnostic views the scene is not replaced by false colours. Its purpose is to settle once and for all whether the horizon band comes from the sky or from the cloud pass: if the band remains with the clouds disabled it is in the sky; if it disappears it is in the clouds. Off for normal play.
