value.COLD_FOG_NIGHT.100 = Same as ground
value.COLD_FOG_NIGHT.160 =暗
value.COLD_FOG_NIGHT.220 =普通
value.COLD_FOG_NIGHT.320 =明亮
value.COLD_FOG_NIGHT.500 =极亮
option.COLD_FOG_NIGHT.comment = How bright the cold fog is at night, as a percentage of the ambient light on the ground. It used to be a fixed colour that knew nothing about the ambient level - depending on moon phase the fog was 9 to 27 times brighter than the ground, making the horizon the brightest surface in a night scene. It is now built from the same source as the terrain lighting, moon phase included. Above 100 percent is correct, because fog gathers scattered light along the whole view distance and is therefore brighter than shadowed ground. The daytime colour is unaffected.
