option.CLOUD_ALT = Clouds: layer altitude
option.CLOUD_ALT.comment = Absolute world height of the cloud layer - and the real reason the clouds looked enormous. It sat at 243 (vanilla cloud height) while the player stands at 70, so the layer was only 173 blocks overhead and a single cloud covered 37 degrees of sky. A fist at arm length is 10 degrees. Size alone could not fix this, because the erosion detail would have ended up nearly as large as the cloud. Photon puts its cumulus at 1200. Higher means the same cloud, just further away - shape, detail and anvil are preserved. The raymarch step count scales along automatically, so it costs no frame rate.
