value.MOON_SURFACE.150 =强
value.MOON_SURFACE.220 =非常强
option.MOON_SURFACE.comment = How clearly maria and craters show on the moon. The maria are the large dark plains that make a moon read as a moon; the craters come from the pack's Worley texture, which yields cells with a bright rim and a dark centre - exactly the shape of a crater. Both are anchored to the moon sphere rather than the screen, so they travel correctly with the phase. They fade out towards the rim of the disc, where the surface is so steeply angled that any feature collapses below pixel size and would only shimmer.
option.MOON_PHASE_CURVE = Moon: phase brightness
value.MOON_PHASE_CURVE.0 = Off (equally bright)
value.MOON_PHASE_CURVE.35 =微妙
value.MOON_PHASE_CURVE.60 =普通
value.MOON_PHASE_CURVE.100 = Real (very dark crescent)
option.MOON_PHASE_CURVE.comment = How much dimmer the moon gets towards a thin crescent. The real moon is disproportionately bright when full: not only because more area is lit, but because at opposition every grain of dust hides its own shadow - lunar dust is retroreflective. Measured, a half moon has half the lit area but only one twelfth of the brightness. Without this curve a crescent is just a cropped full moon and every phase looks equally bright. "Real" applies the measured curve in full and makes a crescent very dark - usually too dark for a game.
option.MOON_EARTHSHINE = Moon: earthshine
value.MOON_EARTHSHINE.0 =关
value.MOON_EARTHSHINE.25 =微妙
value.MOON_EARTHSHINE.45 =普通
value.MOON_EARTHSHINE.75 =强
value.MOON_EARTHSHINE.120 =非常强
option.MOON_EARTHSHINE.comment = The ashen glow on the unlit side of the moon. On a crescent the dark side is not actually black but faintly visible, lit by light the Earth reflects back. Its strength runs opposite to the moon phase: the thinner the crescent, the fuller the Earth stands in the moon's sky. Without it a crescent looks like a cut-out shape; with it, like a photograph.
