option.CLOUD_WISPY.comment = How the worley erosion eats into the cloud. Round = compact cumulus masses. Wispy = the erosion attacks the ridges instead of the valleys and pulls the cloud apart into threads. Costs nothing - it is the same maths with a different sign progression. There are deliberately no intermediate values; there both shapes partly cancel out mathematically.
option.CLOUD_FADE_TO_SKY = Clouds: read distant colour from the sky
option.CLOUD_FADE_TO_SKY.comment = Sets WHICH colour distant clouds fade into. On: the colour is read from the already rendered sky at exactly that spot. Off: it is computed from a second sky formula rebuilt inside the cloud pass that has to be kept in sync with the sky by hand - and measured, it was off by 36 of 255 units. This was NOT the cause of the horizon band; comparing both settings disproved that. It does remove a source of error that can drift apart again at any time. Now that distance acts through colour alone, more depends on it: only if the distant colour is exactly the sky does the distant cloud vanish without trace. Sky pixels only; in front of terrain distant clouds would otherwise take on the ground colour.
